      "instance_name": "Holocaust",
      "label": "Holocaust",
      "description": "The systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. The image depicts prisoners in striped uniforms, characteristic of Nazi concentration camps, which are central to understanding the historical context of the meme. The meme trivializes this genocide by using the image for dark humor.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_4870eb5f"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_dd0d5979",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Nazi_concentration_camps",
      "label": "Nazi concentration camps",
      "description": "Prisons established by Nazi Germany during the Holocaust to imprison, torture, and murder millions of people, including Jews, Roma, disabled individuals, and others deemed undesirable. The striped uniforms and barbed wire in the image are iconic symbols of these camps.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
